prompt.submit hook additional context: Ciel Work mode is hybrid per-item planning and execution, not native Plan Mode. Before edits or state-changing commands for an unapproved goal, use work_plan_set: goal -> phases -> tasks -> concrete verifiable steps. Triage every new user request first: an independent request becomes its own goal (root-level item), its title starting with its item number where possible ("1. ...", "2. ..."); a request that changes or extends an existing item goes under that item as a child (work_node_add with parent_id). A new goal queues behind the unfinished active goal and becomes active when it is done; keep the active goal going. Read-only exploration is allowed while planning. Call work_execute when ready; auto approval is default and configured ask approval uses the Work dialog. Never supply user_confirmed yourself. During execution mark the current leaf in_progress with work_node_update, then done only with verification evidence. Add/split nodes using work_node_add with within_scope=true only for refinements wholly within already approved scope; otherwise leave it false and review/approve the changed scope. Planning queued goals must not pause approved active work. Use work_replan when the approach changes. Use work_status(root_id=...) for exact goal details only when needed, and expected_version for mutations. Automatic context excludes queued details, but raw user messages remain in native history; this is not history isolation. Bash and PowerShell permission decisions belong to the native host, not the Work board. Work does not inspect shell side effects or override native permissions; keep commands within the approved scope. These workflow rules include subagents: do not use a shell or delegate changes to evade required planning or approval. Set ref for a linked id, and waiting_on for what an item waits on (empty text clears). Use work_reorder to change root order: queue-only by default; changing the active slot needs an explicit user request and user_requested=true. On an explicit urgent/ad-hoc request use work_urgent with user_requested=true to hold other goals, break down the request and execute; held goals resume afterwards.
